   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome 1:
1.	The availability of adaptation Taskforce coordination strategy.
2.	The academic study report of the RAN-API status. 
3.	Legal standing for the RAN-API.
4.	Technical guidelines on RAN-API implementation, monitoring and evaluation.
5.	The number of delivered training packages on gender-responsive budget tagging for CCA priorities.
6.	The amount of gender-responsive budget tagging for CCA investment priorities. 

Outcome 2:
1.	The number of validated indicators for CCA priorities identified in the NDC.
2.	The number of training materials for climate risk assessments for CCA priorities identified in the NDC.
3.	The number of government officials, civil society representatives and academia that took part in the training for climate risk assessments.

Outcome 3:
1.	Sum of stakeholders took part in multi-stakeholder consultation assessing capacity needs for climate risk assessments for landscape-based adaptation in Wakatobi. Participants will include selected task force members, the Ministry of Women&#x2019;s Empowerment and Child Protection, BKF and local government and non-government stakeholders (civil society, private sector, academia) from Wakatobi.
2.	The availability of capacity needs assessment report.
3.	The number of developed capacity-building packages for climate risk assessments for landscape-based adaptation approaches. 
4.	Number of participants took part in the training of trainers (ToT) workshops on conducting vulnerability and risk assessments and identifying landscape-based adaptation options in Wakatobi. Participants will include selected task force members, the Ministry of Women&#x2019;s Empowerment and Child Protection, BKF and local government and non-government stakeholders (civil society, private sector, academia) from Wakatobi.
5.	Number of local government and non-government stakeholders (civil society, private sector, academia) from Wakatobi takes part in training for vulnerable communities related to climate risk and impact assessments.
6.	Sum</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 Adaptation Taskforce exists, but needs revitalising and strengthening, with coordination mechanisms enhanced
1.2 Legal standing for RAN-API does not currently exist to govern adaptation unlike the framework for mitigation
1.3 RAN-API of Indon esia has recently been reviewed but needs updating based on developmental priorities, and recent data for thematic areas
1.4 Indonesia has policies established to highlight the need for gender-responsive CCA, and a climate change budgeting system. But there is a need to merge the two concepts for effective implementation of a gender-responsive CCA budget tagging system at the national level. 

2.1 Vulnerability assessment has been conducted by SIDIK at the national level, but the parameters are limited and socio-economic indicators are lacking. Gender data is not incorporated into the risk assessments
2.2 Scientific information that can inform indicators is limited. Currently there is only a prototype for the resilience index rather than an actual index
2.3 Climate risk assessment and gender-responsive risk and vulnerability assessments are relatively new concepts for which capacity is not sufficiently prevalent. Stakeholders do not have the skills and technical expertise necessary to conduct gender-responsive climate risk and vulnerability assessments.

3.1 Climate risk assessment is a new concept which was introduced through the IPCC AR5 report, and which has not yet been implemented by many stakeholders in Indonesia. Among government staff and other stakeholders, capacity for developing risk assessments for climate change impacts is limited.
3.2 For Wakatobi there are no gender-responsive climate risk assessments that have been conducted using landscape-based adaptation approaches 
3.3 Climate budgeting has been introduced in Indonesia for CCA at the national level, but sub-national level CCA budgeting is not practiced. 
3.4 There is no gender-responsive budget tagging system for CCA in Wakatobi</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
